From aeffc5fb9f48bcdb726ebe6beabb67a7dec978f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:49:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] test(emitter): register 136 literal-name and lexical-prologue
 witnesses with the Rust baseline

The 120 proposed commands (literal computed names of decorated methods,
getters, setters and auto-accessors with identifier controls; decimal,
hex and separator numeric keys, plain and escaped template keys and their
string control, a template-keyed method and its substitution control;
function and arrow bodies with and without prologue directives) were split
by group into input fixtures and observed with the existing observer,
twice each: 240 Program executions, 0 diagnostics, 0 exceptions, exit 0.

A reachability extension for the later-pass readers of the hoisted `var`
statement (tsc marks it CustomPrologue) adds `lexical-prologue-readers`:
the top-level undecorated hoist under CommonJS on every configuration and
under AMD/UMD/System at ES2022, plus a parameter-initializer owner of the
same hoist (18 commands; AMD/UMD/System report TS5107 and still emit).
Version 2 of that group keeps the 16 commands the decorator pass owns
(byte-identical inputs and observations); the two System commands stay in
version 1 only, because their JavaScript is already exact and their source
map is the System module transform's (no mappings in the native output).

Rust baseline on the unchanged production (registration only), one
contracts binary per chain, two complete captures per case:
- literal-member-kinds 18/48 exact: method/getter/setter rows on the five
  lowered configurations differ only in the source map end segment of
  `__runInitializers(_a, _staticExtraInitializers);`
- literal-key-spelling 28/48 exact: template keys print "x" instead of
  `x` in the context name and access object; numerics exact
- lexical-prologue 14/24 exact: `var _a;` printed before the directives
- lexical-prologue-readers 2/18 exact: `var _a;` after the __esModule
  marker (CommonJS/AMD/UMD), after class-fields' parameter-default
  statement (parameter rows), System map empty

